    q: "What is a private water supply?"
    a: "Water drawn from your own borehole, spring or well instead of the mains, then stored, treated and pumped on your own property to whatever standard you need."
  - icon: "cycle"
    q: "Why does it matter?"
    a: "No standing charge and no bill that rises every year, no dependence on a mains network that can fail, and water treated to a standard mains supply rarely matches. On an estate or any high-demand property, a supply pays for itself and keeps paying."
  - icon: "gauge"
    q: "What does it take?"
    a: "Every source is different, so the system has to be designed around your water and your demand. Survey and UKAS-accredited analysis first, then filtration, storage and treatment specified for what is actually coming out of the ground."
